.TH cmp 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
cmp \- compare two files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cmp
.I "file1 file2"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cmp
compares the two files and says how they differ.
.SH OPTIONS
None.  There is no
.BR \-s ,
no
.B \-l
and no
.BR \-i .
.SH OUTPUT
.B cmp
is talkative where other systems are silent, and prints one of:
.IP
Files are links to each other
.IP
Files are identical
.IP
Files are different sizes
.IP
First file is shorter than second
.IP
Second file is shorter than first
.IP
Files differ at byte position \fIn\fR
.PP
Byte positions count from zero.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if the files are the same or are links to each other, 1 if they
differ, 2 if a file could not be read.
.SH NOTES
Because there is no quiet option, a script that only wants the exit
status should send the output to
.BR /dev/null .
.PP
Two names for one inode are reported as links without either being read,
so
.B cmp
is the cheap way to find out whether
.B ln
was used.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diff (1),
.BR cksum (1)
